---@class aws.comprehend.DetectDominantLanguageRequest
---@field Text aws.comprehend.CustomerInputString|distilled.Secret A UTF-8 text string. The string must contain at least 20 characters. The maximum string size is 100 KB.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectDominantLanguageResponse
---@field Languages? aws.comprehend.ListOfDominantLanguages Array of languages that Amazon Comprehend detected in the input text. The array is sorted in descending order of the score (the dominant language is always the first element in the array).

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectEntitiesRequest
---@field Text? aws.comprehend.CustomerInputString|distilled.Secret A UTF-8 text string. The maximum string size is 100 KB. If you enter text using this parameter, do not use the Bytes parameter.
---@field LanguageCode? aws.comprehend.LanguageCode|string The language of the input documents. You can specify any of the primary languages supported by Amazon Comprehend. If your request includes the endpoint for a custom entity recognition model, Amazon Comprehend uses the language of your custom model, and it ignores any language code that you specify here.
---@field EndpointArn? aws.comprehend.EntityRecognizerEndpointArn The Amazon Resource Name of an endpoint that is associated with a custom entity recognition model. Provide an endpoint if you want to detect entities by using your own custom model instead of the default model that is used by Amazon Comprehend.
---@field Bytes? aws.comprehend.SemiStructuredDocumentBlob This field applies only when you use a custom entity recognition model that was trained with PDF annotations. For other cases, enter your text input in the Text field.
---@field DocumentReaderConfig? aws.comprehend.DocumentReaderConfig Provides configuration parameters to override the default actions for extracting text from PDF documents and image files.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectEntitiesResponse
---@field Entities? aws.comprehend.ListOfEntities A collection of entities identified in the input text. For each entity, the response provides the entity text, entity type, where the entity text begins and ends, and the level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has in the detection.
---@field DocumentMetadata? aws.comprehend.DocumentMetadata Information about the document, discovered during text extraction. This field is present in the response only if your request used the Byte parameter.
---@field DocumentType? aws.comprehend.ListOfDocumentType The document type for each page in the input document. This field is present in the response only if your request used the Byte parameter.
---@field Blocks? aws.comprehend.ListOfBlocks Information about each block of text in the input document. Blocks are nested. A page block contains a block for each line of text, which contains a block for each word.
---@field Errors? aws.comprehend.ListOfErrors Page-level errors that the system detected while processing the input document. The field is empty if the system encountered no errors.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectKeyPhrasesRequest
---@field Text aws.comprehend.CustomerInputString|distilled.Secret A UTF-8 text string. The string must contain less than 100 KB of UTF-8 encoded characters.
---@field LanguageCode aws.comprehend.LanguageCode|string The language of the input documents. You can specify any of the primary languages supported by Amazon Comprehend. All documents must be in the same language.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectKeyPhrasesResponse
---@field KeyPhrases? aws.comprehend.ListOfKeyPhrases A collection of key phrases that Amazon Comprehend identified in the input text. For each key phrase, the response provides the text of the key phrase, where the key phrase begins and ends, and the level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has in the accuracy of the detection.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectPiiEntitiesRequest
---@field Text aws.comprehend.String A UTF-8 text string. The maximum string size is 100 KB.
---@field LanguageCode aws.comprehend.LanguageCode|string The language of the input text. Enter the language code for English (en) or Spanish (es).

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectPiiEntitiesResponse
---@field Entities? aws.comprehend.ListOfPiiEntities A collection of PII entities identified in the input text. For each entity, the response provides the entity type, where the entity text begins and ends, and the level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has in the detection.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectSentimentRequest
---@field Text aws.comprehend.CustomerInputString|distilled.Secret A UTF-8 text string. The maximum string size is 5 KB.
---@field LanguageCode aws.comprehend.LanguageCode|string The language of the input documents. You can specify any of the primary languages supported by Amazon Comprehend. All documents must be in the same language.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectSentimentResponse
---@field Sentiment? aws.comprehend.SentimentType The inferred sentiment that Amazon Comprehend has the highest level of confidence in.
---@field SentimentScore? aws.comprehend.SentimentScore An object that lists the sentiments, and their corresponding confidence levels.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectSyntaxRequest
---@field Text aws.comprehend.CustomerInputString|distilled.Secret A UTF-8 string. The maximum string size is 5 KB.
---@field LanguageCode aws.comprehend.SyntaxLanguageCode|string The language code of the input documents. You can specify any of the following languages supported by Amazon Comprehend: German ("de"), English ("en"), Spanish ("es"), French ("fr"), Italian ("it"), or Portuguese ("pt").

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectSyntaxResponse
---@field SyntaxTokens? aws.comprehend.ListOfSyntaxTokens A collection of syntax tokens describing the text. For each token, the response provides the text, the token type, where the text begins and ends, and the level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has that the token is correct. For a list of token types, see Syntax in the Comprehend Developer Guide.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectTargetedSentimentRequest
---@field Text aws.comprehend.CustomerInputString|distilled.Secret A UTF-8 text string. The maximum string length is 5 KB.
---@field LanguageCode aws.comprehend.LanguageCode|string The language of the input documents. Currently, English is the only supported language.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectTargetedSentimentResponse
---@field Entities? aws.comprehend.ListOfTargetedSentimentEntities Targeted sentiment analysis for each of the entities identified in the input text.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectToxicContentRequest
---@field TextSegments aws.comprehend.ListOfTextSegments|distilled.Secret A list of up to 10 text strings. Each string has a maximum size of 1 KB, and the maximum size of the list is 10 KB.
---@field LanguageCode aws.comprehend.LanguageCode|string The language of the input text. Currently, English is the only supported language.

---@class aws.comprehend.DetectToxicContentResponse
---@field ResultList? aws.comprehend.ListOfToxicLabels Results of the content moderation analysis. Each entry in the results list contains a list of toxic content types identified in the text, along with a confidence score for each content type. The results list also includes a toxicity score for each entry in the results list.

